PowerScribe One UIA & RP2040 HID Remapper Reference
1. Executive Summary & AI Studio Context
This document serves as a complete architectural and code reference for automating Nuance PowerScribe One (Nuance.PSOne.exe) using AutoHotkey v2 UI Automation (UIA-v2) and emulating a VEC Infinity USB Foot Pedal (VID 0x05F3, PID 0x00FF) on a single RP2040 microcontroller running custom HID Remapper (jfedor2/hid-remapper) firmware.


________________


2. PowerScribe One UI Architecture & AutoHotkey v2 UIA
* Framework: PowerScribe One is built on WPF (Windows Presentation Foundation), whereas older PowerScribe 360 is built on WinForms. Neither uses WinUI.
* Window Class Structure: Top-level windows expose dynamic classes (HwndWrapper[Nuance.PSOne.exe;;...]) rendered inside a single DirectX surface without child Win32 HWND handles.
* Automation Method: Standard Win32 calls (ControlClick, ControlGetText) fail. Automation requires Microsoft UI Automation (IUIAutomation) via Descolada's UIA.ahk (UIA-v2) library targeting AutomationId, Name, and Type.
* WPF Quirks:
   * Some toolbar controls only implement LegacyIAccessiblePattern instead of InvokePattern (fallback: .LegacyIAccessiblePattern.DoDefaultAction() or .ControlClick()).
   * Multi-window floating layouts require narrowing the root handle by title (e.g., PowerScribe One - Report ahk_exe Nuance.PSOne.exe).
AHK v2 UIA Reference Script
